桿與償債","desc":"短期流動性安全 (ΔLiquidity > 0)","passed":0,"detail":"流動比率 = 0.37"},{"id":7,"category":"槓桿與償債","desc":"股本未遭稀釋 (ΔShares ≤ 0)","passed":1,"detail":"未大幅增發新股割韭菜"},{"id":8,"category":"營運效率","desc":"毛利率擴張 (ΔMargin > 0)","passed":0,"detail":"產品定價權增強，毛利結構健康"},{"id":9,"category":"營運效率","desc":"資產週轉率提升 (ΔTurnover > 0)","passed":0,"detail":"每單位資產產出效益改善"}],"fair_val":22.28,"default_fair_val":22.28,"premium_pct":298.7,"is_undervalued":false,"pe_trailing":9.6,"pe_forward":8.4,"pb_trailing":1.5,"pb_forward":1.4,"div_yield":3.85,"ps_ratio":6.6,"fcf_to_ev":1.6,"fcf_to_mcap":3.8,"liab_to_assets":74.5,"cash_to_assets":0.1,"current_ratio":0.37,"roe":15.3,"roa":3.9,"moat":{"ticker":"SR","period":"2026Q3","m1_brand_pricing":{"score":2,"comment_zh":"Spire Inc. 作為一家受監管的公用事業公司，其品牌和定價權受到嚴格的監管。公司無法自由設定價格以最大化利潤，而是必須經過監管機構的批准，這大大削弱了其定價能力。其品牌價值主要體現在可靠的服務供應上，而非強大的市場影響力。與其他消費品或科技公司相比，其品牌在消費者心中缺乏情感連結或獨特性，因此在定價權方面壁壘極為薄弱，難以形成真正的經濟護城河。","comment_en":"As a regulated utility company, Spire Inc.'s brand and pricing power are strictly controlled by regulators. The company cannot freely set prices to maximize profits; instead, price adjustments require regulatory approval, significantly weakening its pricing ability. Its brand value primarily lies in reliable service provision rather than strong market influence. Compared to consumer goods or tech companies, its brand lacks emotional connection or uniqueness in consumers' minds, resulting in an extremely weak barrier in terms of pricing power, making it difficult to form a true economic moat."},"m2_patents_regulatory":{"score":8,"comment_zh":"Spire Inc. 屬於受嚴格監管的公用事業行業，其核心業務——天然氣配送——受到政府特許經營權的保護。這種特許經營權構成了強大的進入壁壘，限制了潛在競爭者進入市場。雖然沒有傳統意義上的專利，但其運營執照和受監管的市場地位，實質上賦予了其在特定地理區域內的壟斷性權利。這種監管環境雖然限制了成長，但也提供了相對穩定的收入來源和顯著的進入壁壘，是其主要的護城河。","comment_en":"Spire Inc. operates in the highly regulated utility sector, and its core business of natural gas distribution is protected by government-granted operating franchises. These franchises create a strong barrier to entry, limiting potential competitors from entering the market. While not possessing traditional patents, its operating licenses and regulated market position effectively grant it monopolistic rights within specific geographic areas. Although this regulatory environment limits growth, it also provides a relatively stable income stream and a significant entry barrier, serving as its primary moat."},"m3_high_switching_costs":{"score":7,"comment_zh":"對於家庭和企業用戶而言，更換天然氣供應商的轉換成本相對較高。這不僅涉及物理上的管道連接和設備安裝，還包括與新供應商重新建立合同、信用檢查以及潛在的服務中斷風險。雖然用戶可以選擇不同的能源來源（如電力），但在現有基礎設施下，更換天然氣供應商的實際操作複雜度和時間成本，為 Spire Inc. 提供了穩固的客戶黏性，構成了重要的轉換成本壁壘。","comment_en":"For residential and business customers, the switching costs associated with changing natural gas suppliers are relatively high. This involves not only physical pipeline connections and equipment installation but also establishing new contracts with a different supplier, credit checks, and potential service interruption risks. While customers can opt for alternative energy sources like electricity, the practical complexity and time costs of switching natural gas providers within the existing infrastructure provide Spire Inc. with solid customer stickiness, forming a significant switching cost barrier."},"m4_network_effects":{"score":1,"comment_zh":"Spire Inc. 的業務模式，即天然氣的傳輸和配送，本質上不具備顯著的網絡效應。其基礎設施（管道網絡）的價值主要在於其物理連接性，而非用戶數量增加帶來的邊際效用遞增。用戶的增加並不會直接提升其他用戶使用該網絡的價值，反之亦然。因此，網絡效應在此類公用事業中幾乎不存在，無法構成有效的經濟護城河。","comment_en":"Spire Inc.'s business model, which involves the transmission and distribution of natural gas, inherently lacks significant network effects. The value of its infrastructure (pipeline network) primarily lies in its physical connectivity, not in the increasing marginal utility derived from a growing user base. An increase in users does not directly enhance the value of the network for other users, and vice versa. Therefore, network effects are virtually non-existent in this type of utility, failing to constitute an effective economic moat."},"m5_cost_advantage_scale":{"score":7,"comment_zh":"作為一家大型的受監管公用事業公司，Spire Inc. 受益於顯著的規模經濟效應。其龐大的基礎設施網絡（管道、儲存設施）攤薄了固定成本，使得單位輸氣成本低於小型競爭者。此外，其採購能力和與供應商的長期合約，也可能帶來一定的成本優勢。雖然監管機構會審核成本，但規模帶來的運營效率和採購議價能力，仍是其重要的成本壁壘。","comment_en":"As a large, regulated utility company, Spire Inc. benefits from significant economies of scale. Its extensive infrastructure network (pipelines, storage facilities) spreads fixed costs, resulting in lower per-unit gas transportation costs compared to smaller competitors. Furthermore, its procurement capabilities and long-term contracts with suppliers may also provide cost advantages. Although regulators review costs, the operational efficiency and purchasing power derived from scale still represent an important cost barrier."},"m6_unique_geography_assets":{"score":8,"comment_zh":"Spire Inc. 在其營運的特定地理區域內擁有獨特的資產和基礎設施。這些天然氣管道網絡是多年投資和建設的結果，對於任何新進入者而言，複製這些資產的成本極高且耗時。其在特定地區的市場滲透率和客戶基礎，構成了難以逾越的地理壁壘。這種對特定區域的深度紮根和基礎設施的壟斷性擁有，是其重要的護城河。","comment_en":"Spire Inc. possesses unique assets and infrastructure within the specific geographic regions it operates. These natural gas pipeline networks are the result of years of investment and construction, making the cost and time required for any new entrant to replicate these assets extremely high. Its market penetration and customer base in these specific areas form an insurmountable geographical barrier. This deep entrenchment in particular regions and the monopolistic ownership of infrastructure constitute a significant moat."},"m7_operational_efficiency":{"score":7,"comment_zh":"Spire Inc. 作為一家成熟的公用事業公司，在運營效率方面通常表現穩健。其標準化的運營流程、對安全和可靠性的高度重視，以及持續的基礎設施維護和升級，都有助於維持高效的運營。儘管受到監管的約束，但通過精細化管理和技術應用來降低運營成本、提高服務質量，是其維持競爭力的關鍵。其在運營效率上的持續投入，構成了穩固的護城河。","comment_en":"As a mature utility company, Spire Inc. typically demonstrates robust operational efficiency. Its standardized operating procedures, strong emphasis on safety and reliability, and continuous infrastructure maintenance and upgrades contribute to maintaining efficient operations. Despite regulatory constraints, reducing operating costs and improving service quality through meticulous management and technology adoption are key to sustaining its competitiveness. Its ongoing investment in operational efficiency forms a solid moat."},"m8_capital_allocation":{"score":6,"comment_zh":"Spire Inc. 的資本配置策略主要圍繞著維護和擴展其受監管的基礎設施，以及支付穩定的股息。雖然其股息支付歷史悠久，顯示了管理層對股東回報的重視，但其增長機會相對有限，且資本支出需求較大。公司在再投資和股息支付之間取得平衡，但相較於能夠進行高回報併購或股票回購的企業，其資本配置的靈活性和創造超額價值的潛力較為有限。","comment_en":"Spire Inc.'s capital allocation strategy primarily revolves around maintaining and expanding its regulated infrastructure, as well as paying stable dividends. While its long history of dividend payments indicates management's focus on shareholder returns, growth opportunities are relatively limited, and capital expenditure requirements are substantial. The company balances reinvestment with dividend payments, but its capital allocation flexibility and potential for creating excess value are somewhat limited compared to companies capable of high-return acquisitions or share buybacks."},"m9_customer_retention":{"score":7,"comment_zh":"如 M3 所述，由於基礎設施的限制和轉換成本，Spire Inc. 在其服務區域內擁有很高的客戶保留率。用戶依賴其提供的天然氣服務來滿足基本需求，且更換供應商的障礙較多。這種客戶黏性使得公司能夠維持穩定的收入流，儘管其增長潛力受限，但客戶的穩定性構成了重要的護城河。","comment_en":"As mentioned in M3, due to infrastructure limitations and switching costs, Spire Inc. enjoys a high customer retention rate within its service areas. Customers rely on its natural gas services for essential needs, and the barriers to switching suppliers are significant. This customer stickiness allows the company to maintain a stable revenue stream. Although its growth potential is limited, customer stability constitutes an important moat."},"m10_durability":{"score":8,"comment_zh":"Spire Inc. 的業務具有高度的持久性。天然氣作為一種重要的能源，在可預見的未來仍將是家庭和工業的關鍵組成部分。儘管面臨來自可再生能源的長期挑戰，但其受監管的業務模式提供了穩定的現金流和對基礎設施的壟斷性權利，使其能夠抵禦經濟週期和行業變革的衝擊。其業務的基礎性和必需性，賦予了其極強的持久性。","comment_en":"Spire Inc.'s business possesses a high degree of durability. Natural gas, as a vital energy source, will remain a key component for households and industries for the foreseeable future. Despite long-term challenges from renewable energy sources, its regulated business model provides stable cash flows and monopolistic rights to its infrastructure, enabling it to withstand the impacts of economic cycles and industry changes. The fundamental and essential nature of its business grants it strong durability."},"overall_moat_verdict_zh":"Spire Inc. 的經濟護城河主要來自其受監管的特許經營權（M2）、顯著的規模經濟（M5）、獨特的地理資產（M6）以及由此產生的客戶黏性（M3, M9）。這些因素共同構成了一個相對穩定的收費橋模式，為公司提供了持久的現金流。然而，其定價權（M1）受限，網絡效應（M4）幾乎為零，這限制了其進一步擴張和創造超額價值的潛力。總體而言，Spire 是一家具有高度持久性但增長有限的公用事業公司，其護城河堅固但非罕見。","overall_moat_verdict_en":"Spire Inc.'s economic moat primarily stems from its regulated operating franchises (M2), significant economies of scale (M5), unique geographical assets (M6), and the resulting customer stickiness (M3, M9). These factors collectively form a relatively stable toll-bridge-like model, providing the company with durable cash flows. However, its pricing power (M1) is limited, and network effects (M4) are virtually non-existent, constraining its potential for further expansion and excess value creation. Overall, Spire is a highly durable but growth-limited utility company with a solid, though not rare, moat.","evidenceHash":"3e1e508487233a105d9eeb62523b3b979b8ed65f3e9f32ebaa2a1b2a7377787f","assessmentPolicy":"buffett-moat-v3","model":"gemini-2.5-flash-lite","provider":"Gemini"},"ratingSources":{"moat":{"reason":null,"evidenceHash":"3e1e508487233a105d9eeb62523b3b979b8ed65f3e9f32ebaa2a1b2a7377787f","currentEvidenceHash":"3e1e508487233a105d9eeb62523b3b979b8ed65f3e9f32ebaa2a1b2a7377787f"},"fScore":{"score":3,"checkedAt":null},"zScore":{"asOfDate":"2025-09-30","period":"FY 2025","basis":"comparableAnnual","model":"z","zone":"distress","reason":null,"scoringCurrency":"USD","applicability":null,"checkedAt":"2026-11-14T07:33:14.971Z","evidenceHash":"9e29f8a348568f7cda3bc0aa418a0b1214d4cc5c5a028720b7b0e16a375c6e4f"},"mScore":{"asOfDate":"2025-09-30","period":"FY 2025","basis":"comparableAnnual","model":null,"zone":"clean","reason":null,"scoringCurrency":"USD","applicability":null,"checkedAt":"2026-11-14T07:33:14.971Z","evidenceHash":"9e29f8a348568f7cda3bc0aa418a0b1214d4cc5c5a028720b7b0e16a375c6e4f"}},"fin_valuation":{"is_financial":false},"image":"https://images.financialmodelingprep.com/symbol/SR.png","logo":"https://images.financialmodelingprep.com/symbol/SR.png","website":"https://www.spireenergy.com","ceo":"Scott E. Doyle","full_time_employees":"3497","description":"Spire Inc. operates as a public utility holding company, which provides natural gas services through its regulated core utility operations while engaging in non-regulated activities. It operates through the following business segments: Gas Utility, Gas Marketing, and Midstream. The Gas Utility segment includes the regulated operations of Spire Missouri, Spire Alabama, Spire Gulf, and Spire Mississippi. The Gas Marketing segment represents the subsidiary, Spire Marketing, which provides non-regulated natural gas marketing services throughout the United States. The Midstream segment consists of Spire STL Pipeline, Spire MoGas Pipeline, Spire Storage West, and Spire Storage Salt Plains, which are subsidiaries engaged in the transportation and storage of natural gas. The company was founded in 1857 and is headquartered in St. Louis, MO.","description_en":"Spire Inc. operates as a public utility holding company, which provides natural gas services through its regulated core utility operations while engaging in non-regulated activities. It operates through the following business segments: Gas Utility, Gas Marketing, and Midstream. The Gas Utility segment includes the regulated operations of Spire Missouri, Spire Alabama, Spire Gulf, and Spire Mississippi. The Gas Marketing segment represents the subsidiary, Spire Marketing, which provides non-regulated natural gas marketing services throughout the United States. The Midstream segment consists of Spire STL Pipeline, Spire MoGas Pipeline, Spire Storage West, and Spire Storage Salt Plains, which are subsidiaries engaged in the transportation and storage of natural gas. The company was founded in 1857 and is headquartered in St. Louis, MO.","description_zh":"Spire Inc.（美股代碼：SR）為 Utilities 領域之重要企業，專注於 Regulated Gas 業務，具備清晰之商業壁壘與現金流創造能力。","address":"700 Market Street","city":"St. Louis","state":"MO","zip":"63101","country":"US","phone":"314 342 0500","full_address":"700 Market Street, St. Louis, MO 63101, US","range_52w":"74.84-95.31","year_high":95.31,"year_low":74.84,"all_time_high":0,"all_time_low":74.84,"inst_ownership_pct":null,"insider_ownership_pct":null,"top_holders":[],"insider_trades":[{"date":"2026-08-12","name":"Krick Timothy W","title":"officer: VP, Chief Accounting Officer","is_buy":null,"action":"A-Award","shares":1230,"price":81.04,"total_val":0.1},{"date":"2026-06-16","name":"Woodard Adam W.","title":"officer: Treasurer","is_buy":null,"action":"I-Discretionary","shares":1100,"price":78.65,"total_val":0.09},{"date":"2026-06-12","name":"KOONCE PAUL D","title":"director","is_buy":true,"action":"P-Purchase","shares":500,"price":78.46,"total_val":0.04},{"date":"2026-06-10","name":"Hyman Ryan L","title":"officer: SVP, CCIO","is_buy":false,"action":"S-Sale","shares":3822,"price":80.51,"total_val":0.31},{"date":"2026-06-04","name":"KOONCE PAUL D","title":"director","is_buy":true,"action":"P-Purchase","shares":500,"price":80.5,"total_val":0.04},{"date":"2026-05-11","name":"KOONCE PAUL D","title":"director","is_buy":true,"action":"P-Purchase","shares":2000,"price":85.81,"total_val":0.17},{"date":"2026-02-17","name":"KOONCE PAUL D","title":"director","is_buy":null,"action":"J-Other","shares":8846,"price":25,"total_val":0.22},{"date":"2026-02-09","name":"Newberry Brenda D","title":"director","is_buy":null,"action":"A-Award","shares":1640,"price":85.27,"total_val":0.14},{"date":"2026-02-09","name":